00:00:01.829 --> 00:00:03.270 align:start position:0%
a year and a half after cambridge  graduates jack merritt  and saskia jones lost their lives we are  for the first time  seeing footage from inside fishmonger's  hall of attacker  asman khan at an event that had been  about rehabilitating prisoners  he can be seen here in the distance  talking to 23 year old volunteer  saskia jones they were sitting just two  seats away from each other  moments before he stabbed her to death  jack merritt though  was the first to lose his life after a  break outside  he returned to the bathroom where in a  cubicle  khan had stashed a black bag and tied  two knives to his hands  police believe the arabic word for allah  had been scratched onto the eight-inch  blade  khan was ready when jack merritt arrived  and it was there that he stabbed the 25  year old to death  jack's mother and merit told the inquest  that he was a good person  she said jack was forced for good in the  world someone who made other people's  lives better for knowing him  she said his death was a tragedy but his  life a triumph  saskia jones meanwhile was taking part  in a breakout event  she also went on a break outside when  she re-entered  khan had emerged from the bathroom he  stabbed her once in the neck by the  cloakroom  today in a statement her family said  that it would be her hope  that no other family is devastated and  heartbroken again in similar  circumstances  they said she should be defined as  someone who battled to improve the lives  of others  in several spheres and was driven to  make real changes in the world  some of the footage that was shown to  the inquest was just too graphic to be  released  we saw images of jack merritt falling  against the door at the entrance to  fishmonger's hall with blood on his  shirt  and then usman khan moments later  fleeing out towards london bridge with  two knives attached to his hands  when khan fled fishmonger's hall he was  being pursued by ministry of justice  employee with a narwhal tusk  and an ex-convict with a fire  extinguisher polish kitchen worker lucas  seen here at the top was injured trying  to control khan  six minutes after the attack began  police fired their first shots khan had  been wearing a fake  explosive belt that the inquest heard  had been made of xbox components  and bandages wrapped in cling film usman  khan  died at the scene on london bridge the  inquest  into his death will begin once the jury  have considered the deaths of two young  graduates  whose lies were cut short ali fulski sky  news
 

